cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  graph_geometry: a plugin architecture for discrete
  curvature and curvature flow on networks
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Xin
    family-names: Lai
    email: laixin@bimsa.cn
    affiliation: >-
      Beijing Institute of Mathematical Sciences and Applications;
      Yau Mathematical Sciences Center, Tsinghua University
repository-code: 'https://github.com/laiguzi/graph-geometry'
abstract: >-
  A Python package in which discrete Ricci curvature
  definitions and Ricci flow equations are plugins:
  optimal-transport curvatures are expressed as four
  swappable components, any other curvature as a single
  function honouring one result contract, and flow
  equations as four-argument callables or typed
  math/LaTeX expressions. Definitions register under a
  name and are usable identically from the Python API, a
  YAML experiment file, and an interactive interface.
keywords:
  - Ricci curvature
  - Ricci flow
  - network geometry
  - optimal transport
  - graph theory
